data bind_and_match_binders_not_typed_from_their_dependency_sibling: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "bind_and_match_binders_not_typed_from_their_dependency_sibling" as NonEmptyStr,
  rung: RungUnread { cause: CurrentRungUnstatedAfterClimb },

  receipts: [
    "HISTORICAL, BOTH POPULATIONS CLIMBED (see the 2026-10-13 receipt below and the match half retired 2026-10-15 with rung drop match_arm_binder_typing_lost_to_lexical_carrier); no residual population remains. THE STATE AS FOUND: two behavior rows bound a name whose type is fixed by a SIBLING child's settled result, and v2.compiler.infer types neither binder from it. An unannotated `let x = e` binds x in the Bind's body, but x's LexicalBinding declares no type (v2.compiler.infer infer_lexical_reference_facts reads binding.declared Absent and leaves the reference underived), although the bound value e was folded in the same row. A match-arm pattern binder is typed by the scrutinee's settled type and the matched variant, and the binder-typing for it is #12641's subject (v2.test.claim.field_projection.field_projection_stages fps_a_match_binder_receiver_is_typed_holds, formerly recording it as not yet inferring). HARM: a projection or application off such a binder stays on the counted frontier or refuses for missing evidence instead of being judged -- loud, never fabricated, but valid programs do not type. This is the same class as gunbc.recurring_failure_mode infer_child_context_cannot_depend_on_a_sibling_result, whose collection-fold case is climbed; these two rows were its remaining population, now climbed.",
    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS: the traversal is no longer the obstacle. v2.std.node fold_node_dependent lets a row schedule its dependency child first and derive the dependent child's context from the parent accumulator, and v2.compiler.infer infer_gather_child_context already does so for a fold-realized Loop. What these rows lack is the BINDING SIDE: a Bind's binder carries no type variable for a frame to instantiate (the fold step's member formal does, minted by function-value lowering), and the match-arm binder's relation to the scrutinee is variant-and-field-indexed rather than one member type. So reusing the driver is necessary and not sufficient, and building either row's frame here, without its binder carrier, would be a frame nothing reads (DESIGN section 3c).",
    "RUNG FOUND AT: mitigatable -- refused or left underived, never wrong. CEILING: structurally guaranteed; both relations are decidable from the sibling's settled type. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, NAMING THE CAPABILITY: a Bind binder carries its own type position (declared or fresh), and infer_gather_child_context schedules the bound value before the body and instantiates that position from the value's settled type for the body subtree only; and a match-arm binder is instantiated from the scrutinee's settled type through the matched variant's field, scheduled the same way -- SUFFICIENT FOR `let r = n; r.children` and a match-arm binder's projection to type through the one frame, with no second parameter-typing route.",
    "LET CLIMBED, 2026-10-13 (native-seven g_fatal_at's `let fatal = diagnostics_fatal(d: d)`). THE TRIGGER'S DESIGN PREDICTION IS SUPERSEDED: the row above predicted that a Bind binder would carry its own type position (declared or fresh) for a frame to instantiate. It needed none. The binder-site InferBinderType frame that match arms already use is keyed by the binder SITE, and v2.compiler.lexical_scope bind_binder is the reader resolve sites a let binder with, so the let half climbed through that existing frame with no new binder carrier. v2.compiler.infer infer_gather_child_context enters an ordinary let's body under infer_let_body_frame -- one row typed by the value's settled type, or by the annotation where one is authored (the value is then evidence judged at PositionLetAnnotation, never the binder's type) -- and infer_gather_let_result_row gives the Bind its body's settled type. The binder key is binding syntax (v2.std.node bind_key_edge), declined by infer's gather and by v2.std.type_binder node_inferred_subtree_nodes as a match arm's pattern is. Resolve's LexicalValued node is not read: it is the value before its own subtree was resolved, so it is not an entry key. A value with no derived type adds no row and the reference stays counted on the frontier. Claims: v2.test.claim.compiler.let_binder_frame. THE TWO POPULATIONS CLIMBED BY SEPARATE IMPLEMENTATIONS: the match half earlier, through the match-arm payload binder frame (infer_match_arm_child_frame); the let half here, through infer_let_body_frame and infer_gather_let_result_row. The match half's evidence was flipped to regression controls 2026-10-15 (rung drop match_arm_binder_typing_lost_to_lexical_carrier retired): field_projection_stages fps_a_match_binder_receiver_is_typed_holds and match_binder_typing mbt_the_binder_is_typed_from_its_variant_field_holds.",
  ],
  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.std.node", decl_name: "fold_node_dependent", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.compiler.infer", decl_name: "infer_gather_child_context", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.compiler.infer", decl_name: "infer_lexical_reference_facts", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.compiler.infer", decl_name: "infer_let_body_frame", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.compiler.infer", decl_name: "infer_gather_let_result_row", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.std.node", decl_name: "bind_key_edge", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.compiler.let_binder_frame", decl_name: "lbf_a_let_reference_and_the_let_take_the_bound_type", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.field_projection.field_projection_stages", decl_name: "fps_a_match_binder_receiver_is_typed_holds", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
